1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,300
In any right triangle you draw,

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:05,260
a squared plus b squared equals c squared.

3
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:07,420
Why does it always work?

4
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:09,580
Squared means an actual square:

5
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,620
a squared is the area of a square with side a.

6
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,380
Try three, four, five.

7
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:17,020
The square on three holds nine little squares,

8
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:18,700
the one on four, sixteen.

9
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:22,060
Together, twenty-five: the square on the long side.

10
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:23,580
But that's one triangle.

11
00:00:23,510 --> 00:00:26,300
For every case, put four identical triangles

12
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:28,860
inside a square with sides a plus b.

13
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:31,820
That leaves a tilted square in the middle, side c.

14
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:34,220
Now slide two of them, without turning.

15
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:37,820
The gap becomes two squares: a squared and b squared.

16
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:41,500
Same square, same triangles: the gaps must match.

17
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:44,860
Which means c squared equals a squared plus b squared.

18
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:47,740
Flat or tall, any right triangle works.

19
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:50,620
The gap just changes shape, never its area.

20
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:51,420
That's why
